Date: Tue, 26 Jan 93 17:43:17 PST
From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: ECON: Paper Losses

I yield!

(no pun intended)

Both Perry Metzger and Glen Raphael have convinced my that my "paper
losses" are not real, where by "paper" I actually meant "potential."

Psychologically, though, there's something more real about not getting
$100 for a stock because one wrote a covered call (an agreement to
deliver shares at some price when one already owns the shares) at $70
than there is when one fails to buy the stock at $70 and then see it
go to $100.

I don't know why this psychological reaction is the way it is, or,
indeed, if others ever feel the same way.

Thanks,

-Tim


